.TH CHANGELOG-LICENSE 8 "July 2026" "changelog 1.0.0" "System Administration Commands"
.SH NAME
changelog license \- print the CYMERTEK Source-Available License embedded in the binary
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B changelog license
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The \fBlicense\fR command displays the full text of the CYMERTEK Source-Available License (CSAL) that governs use and distribution of this software. The license is embedded directly in the binary during build time using Go's \fI//go:embed\fR directive, ensuring users always see the correct version without requiring external file access.

This command is useful for verifying licensing terms before commercial use, including educational institutions and training environments that may require separate licenses.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Show help message and exit.

.TP
\fB-V\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Print the complete license text including all sections and legal disclaimers. Without this flag, only a summary may be displayed (depending on terminal capabilities).
.SH LICENSE SUMMARY
.PP
The CYMERTEK Source-Available License (CSAL) v1.0 grants:

.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
\fIEvaluation Use:\fR Free for personal evaluation, testing, and learning in non-fee-based environments
.IP \(bu 2
\fICommercial Restrictions:\fR Requires separate Commercial License from CYMERTEK for business use, SaaS offerings, paid courses, or any environment collecting fees
.IP \(bu 2
\fIForking:\fR Permitted with proper attribution and unofficial labeling requirements
.RE

.TP
.B Key Sections Covered:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
License Grant and evaluation-only restrictions
.IP \(bu 2
Commercial Use definitions and licensing requirements
.IP \(bu 2
Contribution terms and assignment of rights
.IP \(bu 2
Fork and derivative work obligations
.IP \(bu 2
Trademark and nominative use disclaimers
.IP \(bu 2
Warranty disclaimer and limitation of liability
.RE

